    "text": "The conductivity of a weak acid<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HA</mi></math> of concentration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>(</mo><mi>HA</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>190</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> the ionization constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mfenced></math> of HA is equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />(Round off to the Nearest Integer)"
